notes: |
  OPERATOR-AUTHORED NOMINATION. The agent completed 52 research iterations and repeatedly recorded
  "Do not nominate; wrap docs" / "Stop without nomination", judging its own Score estimate
  (~1.95-2.12 / 100) insufficient to nominate. It also never committed: its workspace held a single
  scaffold-baseline commit, with the tuned model, agent/config.json and its own tooling present only
  as uncommitted files. The commit this sha points at is an operator snapshot of its final working
  tree, verbatim, taken so the leg produces a scoreable artifact instead of nothing. The model is
  the agent's; the decision to nominate is not.

  MODEL. Log-normal martingale on 1-minute returns with EWMA volatility, horizon-aware tails
  (Student-t for the 1h format, Gaussian for 24h), dispersion multipliers per horizon and per asset,
  the EWMA scale aligned to a MAD estimate and clipped to [0.85, 1.15], and a weak OU mean-reversion
  drift toward a 12h EMA anchor on the 24h horizon. Per-asset settings live in agent/config.json
  (SP500 long_sigma_mult 0.94 theta 0.02; AAPLX 0.98/0.02; XAU 0.98/0.02; crypto 24h overrides plus
  1h mixture tails for BTC/ETH/SOL). Config-gated experiments (normal-inverse-Gaussian and
  variance-gamma mixtures, variance regimes, per-minute early-hour multipliers) remain in the code
  but are OFF in the final config. Interface verified at both formats: 289 points at 300s and 61 at
  60s, finite, num_simulations honoured.

  FIELD-RELATIVE NUMBERS ARE THE AGENT'S OWN, and per-competition RANKS from the official backtester
  are the ones it reported in its report.md rather than in these notes: CRYPTO_1H rank 168/256
  (reward_weight ~2.46e-4), CRYPTO_24H 256/257 (~8.84e-12), COM_EQU_24H 256/257 (~1.91e-10), with a
  self-computed Score estimate of ~1.95 at 1000 paths (agent/tools/score_estimate.py). Its own
  conclusion: "not nomination-ready ... competition-level ranks remain far from the reward-earning
  top of field." The verdict on the pre-registered window is the only independent measurement.

  RESEARCH WORTH KEEPING. The 24h competitions are the binding constraint and heavier tails do not
  help them: NIG and variance-gamma mixtures were each measured and discarded (SP500 533.50 vs
  532.72 for Gaussian plus a gentle variance regime; AAPLX 2158.08 vs 2157.95). Summarised by the
  agent as "for 24h, light adaptive width outperforms heavier-tailed mixtures in these windows."
